nts.roster.shipped_with_plugin\",\"title\":\"Installing the plugin installs its three agents\",\"lifecycle\":\"active\",\"value_tier\":\"core\",\"journey_role\":\"golden\",\"usage_frequency\":\"common\",\"tags\":[\"agents\",\"packaging\",\"hosts\",\"no-edge-path\"],\"source_refs\":[{\"kind\":\"file\",\"path\":\"packages/core/src/agents/canonicalAgents.ts\"},{\"kind\":\"file\",\"path\":\"agents/use-cases-updater.md\"},{\"kind\":\"file\",\"path\":\"agents/use-cases-demo-prep.md\"},{\"kind\":\"file\",\"path\":\"agents/use-cases-demo.md\"},{\"kind\":\"file\",\"path\":\".claude-plugin/plugin.json\"},{\"kind\":\"file\",\"path\":\"package.json\"}],\"actor\":\"script\",\"intent\":\"Confirm the agents directory holds exactly the canonical roster, and that both the Claude plugin manifest and the published package actually ship it.\",\"preconditions\":[\"The plugin declares a canonical agent roster in CANONICAL_AGENTS.\"],\"trigger\":\"A release or install gate checks the plugin's shipped surfaces.\",\"scenarios\":[{\"id\":\"agents.roster.shipped_with_plugin.golden_declared\",\"kind\":\"steps\",\"steps\":[\"Read the agents directory and compare it to CANONICAL_AGENTS.\",\"Confirm the Claude plugin manifest declares ./agents.\",\"Confirm the published package files list includes agents.\"],\"observable_outcomes\":[\"The agents directory holds exactly the canonical roster, no more and no less.\",\"A user installing the plugin can dispatch all three agents by name.\"]},{\"id\":\"agents.roster.shipped_with_plugin.bad_roster_entry_without_a_body\",\"kind\":\"steps\",\"steps\":[\"Add a name to CANONICAL_AGENTS with no matching body file.\",\"Run the gate.\"],\"observable_outcomes\":[\"An agent added to the roster without a body fails the gate.\",\"The roster and the directory are held equal in both directions.\"]},{\"id\":\"agents.roster.shipped_with_plugin.bad_body_shipped_without_being_declared\",\"kind\":\"steps\",\"steps\":[\"Add a body file to the agents directory that the roster does not name.\",\"Run the gate.\"],\"observable_outcomes\":[\"An agent shipped without being declared fails the gate.\",\"A body cannot reach users on one host while being invisible to the roster.\"]}],\"observable_outcomes\":[\"An agent added to the roster without a body, or shipped without being declared, fails the gate.\",\"A user installing the plugin can dispatch all three agents by name.\"],\"host_applicability\":[{\"host_surface\":\"claude.cli\",\"supported\":true}],\"verification_policy\":{\"mode\":\"requirements\",\"verifiers\":{\"script\":{\"kind\":\"script\",\"evidence_kind\":\"test_result\",\"command\":[\"pnpm\",\"-s\",\"vitest\",\"run\",\"tests/blackbox/agents-roster.test.ts\",\"-t\",\"agents.roster.shipped_with_plugin\"],\"inputs\":[\"tests/blackbox/agents-roster.test.ts\"]}},\"requirements\":[{\"evidence_kind\":\"test_result\",\"required_verifiers\":[\"script\"],\"minimum_count\":1}]},\"approval_policy\":{\"mode\":\"none\"}}","expected_semantic_hash":"sha256:71cce200b293440ba020c9116d310930a63bbc88e0acb1dc00df9d350746c3c4"},"result":{"schema_version":1,"operation":"upsert","status":"updated","use_case_id":"agents.roster.shipped_with_plugin","file_path":"use-cases/agents/roster.yml","before_hash":"sha256:71cce200b293440ba020c9116d310930a63bbc88e0acb1dc00df9d350746c3c4","after_hash":"sha256:71cce200b293440ba020c9116d310930a63bbc88e0acb1dc00df9d350746c3c4","diagnostics":[]},"written_sha256":"sha256:f6a16ca901aa2fe04e4ba633b1d2ec31e03c67b77de9379061b8377f2fb808e8","written_length":10826,"written_text":"schema_version: 1\nfeature:\n  id: agents.roster\n  name: Shipped agents\n  summary: Ship the three use-case agents (updater, demo-prep, demo) with the plugin so every install gets the same loop \u2014 keep the matrix true, stage a demo, perform it \u2014 instead of each user rebuilding them privately.\nuse_cases:\n  - id: agents.roster.shipped_with_plugin\n    title: Installing the plugin installs its three agents\n    lifecycle: active\n    value_tier: core\n    journey_role: golden\n    usage_frequency: common\n    tags:\n      - agents\n      - packaging\n      - hosts\n      - no-edge-path\n    source_refs:\n      - kind: file\n        path: packages/core/src/agents/canonicalAgents.ts\n      - kind: file\n        path: agents/use-cases-updater.md\n      - kind: file\n        path: agents/use-cases-demo-prep.md\n      - kind: file\n        path: agents/use-cases-demo.md\n      - kind: file\n        path: .claude-plugin/plugin.json\n      - kind: file\n        path: package.json\n    actor: script\n    intent: Confirm the agents directory holds exactly the canonical roster, and that both the Claude plugin manifest and the published package actually ship it.\n    preconditions:\n      - The plugin declares a canonical agent roster in CANONICAL_AGENTS.\n    trigger: A release or install gate checks the plugin's shipped surfaces.\n    scenarios:\n      - id: agents.roster.shipped_with_plugin.golden_declared\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Read the agents directory and compare it to CANONICAL_AGENTS.\n          - Confirm the Claude plugin manifest declares ./agents.\n          - Confirm the published package files list includes agents.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - The agents directory holds exactly the canonical roster, no more and no less.\n          - A user installing the plugin can dispatch all three agents by name.\n      - id: agents.roster.shipped_with_plugin.bad_roster_entry_without_a_body\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Add a name to CANONICAL_AGENTS with no matching body file.\n          - Run the gate.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - An agent added to the roster without a body fails the gate.\n          - The roster and the directory are held equal in both directions.\n      - id: agents.roster.shipped_with_plugin.bad_body_shipped_without_being_declared\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Add a body file to the agents directory that the roster does not name.\n          - Run the gate.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - An agent shipped without being declared fails the gate.\n          - A body cannot reach users on one host while being invisible to the roster.\n    observable_outcomes:\n      - An agent added to the roster without a body, or shipped without being declared, fails the gate.\n      - A user installing the plugin can dispatch all three agents by name.\n    host_applicability:\n      - host_surface: claude.cli\n        supported: true\n    verification_policy:\n      mode: requirements\n      verifiers:\n        script:\n          kind: script\n          evidence_kind: test_result\n          command:\n            - pnpm\n            - -s\n            - vitest\n            - run\n            - tests/blackbox/agents-roster.test.ts\n            - -t\n            - agents.roster.shipped_with_plugin\n          inputs:\n            - tests/blackbox/agents-roster.test.ts\n      requirements:\n        - evidence_kind: test_result\n          required_verifiers:\n            - script\n          minimum_count: 1\n    approval_policy:\n      mode: none\n  - id: agents.roster.bodies_hold_the_line\n    title: An agent body cannot claim approval or cite a command that does not exist\n    lifecycle: active\n    value_tier: critical\n    journey_role: edge\n    usage_frequency: occasional\n    tags:\n      - agents\n      - trust\n      - diagnostics\n    source_refs:\n      - kind: file\n        path: tests/agents/canonical-agents.test.ts\n      - kind: file\n        path: packages/core/src/cli/knownCommands.ts\n    actor: script\n    intent: Hold every shipped agent body to the same rules the skills obey \u2014 parseable frontmatter, only real CLI commands, no authority to claim the user's approval, and no reference to one author's private setup.\n    preconditions:\n      - The plugin ships agent bodies that instruct other agents.\n    trigger: A change to any shipped agent body, or to the CLI command surface it cites.\n    scenarios:\n      - id: agents.roster.bodies_hold_the_line.golden_frontmatter_matches_the_filename\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Parse each agent's YAML frontmatter.\n          - Compare its name with the filename.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - Every shipped agent opens with parseable frontmatter whose name matches its filename.\n      - id: agents.roster.bodies_hold_the_line.bad_cites_a_command_the_cli_does_not_ship\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Extract every use-cases command the body cites.\n          - Check each against the shared allowlist.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - A body that sends the reader to a command the CLI does not ship fails the gate.\n      - id: agents.roster.bodies_hold_the_line.bad_claims_the_users_approval\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Check the body for text authorising an agent to claim user approval or sign-off.\n          - Check it for text calling a generated plan, walkthrough, capsule or runbook proof.\n          - Check it for a claim that host support is verified.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - A body that authorises an agent to claim the user's sign-off fails the gate.\n          - A body that calls prepared material proof fails the same way.\n      - id: agents.roster.bodies_hold_the_line.bad_names_one_authors_private_setup\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Check the body for references to a private roster, a home path, or a sibling repo.\n          - Run the gate.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - A body naming agent-setup, a ~/.claude path or an absolute /Users/ path fails the gate.\n          - Agent bodies ship to everyone who installs the plugin, so one author's machine is meaningless to them.\n      - id: agents.roster.bodies_hold_the_line.edge_description_is_specific_enough_to_route_on\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Read each agent's frontmatter description.\n          - Check it is a string, long enough to carry a trigger, and not a bare restatement of the name.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - A description that merely restates the agent's name fails, because it tells a dispatching agent nothing about when to reach for it.\n    observable_outcomes:\n      - A body that sends the reader to a command the CLI does not ship fails the gate.\n      - A body that authorises an agent to claim the user's sign-off fails the gate.\n    host_applicability:\n      - host_surface: claude.cli\n        supported: true\n    verification_policy:\n      mode: requirements\n      verifiers:\n        script:\n          kind: script\n          evidence_kind: test_result\n          command:\n            - pnpm\n            - -s\n            - vitest\n            - run\n            - tests/blackbox/agents-roster.test.ts\n            - -t\n            - agents.roster.bodies_hold_the_line\n          inputs:\n            - tests/blackbox/agents-roster.test.ts\n      requirements:\n        - evidence_kind: test_result\n          required_verifiers:\n            - script\n          minimum_count: 1\n    approval_policy:\n      mode: none\n  - id: agents.roster.command_allowlist_tracks_cli\n    title: The command allowlist cannot drift from the real CLI\n    lifecycle: active\n    value_tier: supporting\n    journey_role: edge\n    usage_frequency: rare\n    tags:\n      - agents\n      - skills\n      - cli\n    source_refs:\n      - kind: file\n        path: packages/core/src/cli/knownCommands.ts\n      - kind: file\n        path: packages/cli/src/command/registry.ts\n    actor: script\n    intent: Guarantee the allowlist used to validate skill and agent prose equals what the CLI registry actually dispatches, so a correct body is never flagged and a fictional command is never waved through.\n    preconditions:\n      - Skill and agent bodies are validated against a shared command allowlist.\n    trigger: A command is added to or removed from the CLI registry.\n    scenarios:\n      - id: agents.roster.command_allowlist_tracks_cli.golden_nested_command_parity\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Derive every dispatchable nested command path from the CLI registry.\n          - Compare it against the shared allowlist.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - Every dispatchable nested command is allowed in skill and agent bodies.\n          - A skill or agent citing a real command is never reported as unknown.\n      - id: agents.roster.command_allowlist_tracks_cli.golden_flat_command_parity\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Derive every dispatchable flat command from the CLI registry.\n          - Compare it against the allowlist plus the bespoke builtins.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - Every dispatchable flat command is allowed, along with the bespoke builtins.\n      - id: agents.roster.command_allowlist_tracks_cli.bad_registry_command_missing_from_the_allowlist\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Add a command to the CLI registry without adding it to the allowlist.\n          - Run the parity gate.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - Adding a registry command without the allowlist fails the gate.\n          - The allowlist cannot drift from what the CLI actually dispatches.\n      - id: agents.roster.command_allowlist_tracks_cli.edge_the_commands_that_exposed_the_drift\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Check impact and showcase request-approval against the allowlist.\n          - Confirm both are allowed.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - The two commands that had already drifted are allowed, so the regression that prompted this gate stays fixed.\n    observable_outcomes:\n      - Adding a registry command without the allowlist fails the gate.\n      - A skill or agent citing a real command is never reported as unknown.\n    host_applicability:\n      - host_surface: claude.cli\n        supported: true\n    verification_policy:\n      mode: requirements\n      verifiers:\n        script:\n          kind: script\n          evidence_kind: test_result\n          command:\n            - pnpm\n            - -s\n            - vitest\n            - run\n            - tests/blackbox/agents-roster.test.ts\n            - -t\n            - agents.roster.command_allowlist_tracks_cli\n          inputs:\n            - tests/blackbox/agents-roster.test.ts\n      requirements:\n        - evidence_kind: test_result\n          required_verifiers:\n            - script\n          minimum_count: 1\n    approval_policy:\n      mode: none\n","unchanged_from_input":true},{"path":"use-cases/agents/roster.yml","kind":"one_field","options":{"operation":"upsert","target_file":"agents/roster.yml","use_case_json":"{\"id\":\"agents.roster.shipped_with_plugin\",\"title\":\"Installing the plugin installs its three agents (edited)\",\"lifecycle\":\"active\",\"value_tier\":\"core\",\"journey_role\":\"golden\",\"usage_frequency\":\"common\",\"tags\":[\"agents\",\"packaging\",\"hosts\",\"no-edge-path\"],\"source_refs\":[{\"kind\":\"file\",\"path\":\"packages/core/src/agents/canonicalAgents.ts\"},{\"kind\":\"file\",\"path\":\"agents/use-cases-updater.md\"},{\"kind\":\"file\",\"path\":\"agents/use-cases-demo-prep.md\"},{\"kind\":\"file\",\"path\":\"agents/use-cases-demo.md\"},{\"kind\":\"file\",\"path\":\".claude-plugin/plugin.json\"},{\"kind\":\"file\",\"path\":\"package.json\"}],\"actor\":\"script\",\"intent\":\"Confirm the agents directory holds exactly the canonical roster, and that both the Claude plugin manifest and the published package actually ship it.\",\"preconditions\":[\"The plugin declares a canonical agent roster in CANONICAL_AGENTS.\"],\"trigger\":\"A release or install gate checks the plugin's shipped surfaces.\",\"scenarios\":[{\"id\":\"agents.roster.shipped_with_plugin.golden_declared\",\"kind\":\"steps\",\"steps\":[\"Read the agents directory and compare it to CANONICAL_AGENTS.\",\"Confirm the Claude plugin manifest declares ./agents.\",\"Confirm the published package files list includes agents.\"],\"observable_outcomes\":[\"The agents directory holds exactly the canonical roster, no more and no less.\",\"A user installing the plugin can dispatch all three agents by name.\"]},{\"id\":\"agents.roster.shipped_with_plugin.bad_roster_entry_without_a_body\",\"kind\":\"steps\",\"steps\":[\"Add a name to CANONICAL_AGENTS with no matching body file.\",\"Run the gate.\"],\"observable_outcomes\":[\"An agent added to the roster without a body fails the gate.\",\"The roster and the directory are held equal in both directions.\"]},{\"id\":\"agents.roster.shipped_with_plugin.bad_body_shipped_without_being_declared\",\"kind\":\"steps\",\"steps\":[\"Add a body file to the agents directory that the roster does not name.\",\"Run the gate.\"],\"observable_outcomes\":[\"An agent shipped without being declared fails the gate.\",\"A body cannot reach users on one host while being invisible to the roster.\"]}],\"observable_outcomes\":[\"An agent added to the roster without a body, or shipped without being declared, fails the gate.\",\"A user installing the plugin can dispatch all three agents by name.\"],\"host_applicability\":[{\"host_surface\":\"claude.cli\",\"supported\":true}],\"verification_policy\":{\"mode\":\"requirements\",\"verifiers\":{\"script\":{\"kind\":\"script\",\"evidence_kind\":\"test_result\",\"command\":[\"pnpm\",\"-s\",\"vitest\",\"run\",\"tests/blackbox/agents-roster.test.ts\",\"-t\",\"agents.roster.shipped_with_plugin\"],\"inputs\":[\"tests/blackbox/agents-roster.test.ts\"]}},\"requirements\":[{\"evidence_kind\":\"test_result\",\"required_verifiers\":[\"script\"],\"minimum_count\":1}]},\"approval_policy\":{\"mode\":\"none\"}}"},"result":{"schema_version":1,"operation":"upsert","status":"updated","use_case_id":"agents.roster.shipped_with_plugin","file_path":"use-cases/agents/roster.yml","before_hash":"sha256:71cce200b293440ba020c9116d310930a63bbc88e0acb1dc00df9d350746c3c4","after_hash":"sha256:96f28512119e00435b6d675228a37a56021ed0f38dbb5cca8951bf8865ac4476","diagnostics":[]},"written_sha256":"sha256:05d9de8c441dfe1f6b292e28a74ef0172f2098fbc74938114add14adf55e9b65","written_length":10835,"unchanged_from_input":false},{"path":"use-cases/agents/roster.yml","kind":"removed","options":{"operation":"remove","use_case_id":"agents.roster.shipped_with_plugin","reason":"Corpus removal.","expected_semantic_hash":"sha256:71cce200b293440ba020c9116d310930a63bbc88e0acb1dc00df9d350746c3c4"},"result":{"schema_version":1,"operation":"remove","status":"removed","use_case_id":"agents.roster.shipped_with_plugin","file_path":"use-cases/agents/roster.yml","before_hash":"sha256:71cce200b293440ba020c9116d310930a63bbc88e0acb1dc00df9d350746c3c4","after_hash":"sha256:944a6ccdd29b3b6d6c1f209e0927f6f989fdccb8f8589c106fb2af2656b245e9","diagnostics":[]},"written_sha256":"sha256:88bc620a8b1773e4c6337f43794999a0c54ed94509f43157cc1fc0d933d54629","written_length":10967,"unchanged_from_input":false},{"path":"use-cases/capsule/demos.yml","kind":"unchanged","options":{"operation":"upsert","target_file":"capsule/demos.yml","use_case_json":"{\"id\":\"capsule.demos.persisted_smoke_runbook\",\"title\":\"Persisted smoke demo runbook\",\"lifecycle\":\"active\",\"value_tier\":\"core\",\"journey_role\":\"golden\",\"usage_frequency\":\"common\",\"tags\":[\"capsules\",\"smoke\",\"runbook\"],\"source_refs\":[{\"kind\":\"file\",\"path\":\"docs/showcase.md\"},{\"kind\":\"file\",\"path\":\"packages/core/src/capsules/loadCapsule.ts\"}],\"actor\":\"agent\",\"intent\":\"Provide a reusable capsule that references use-case IDs and supports repeatable demos.\",\"preconditions\":[\"A common smoke or golden path deserves a persisted runbook.\"],\"trigger\":\"Agent or user wants a repeatable demonstration without reselecting rows manually.\",\"scenarios\":[{\"id\":\"capsule.demos.persisted_smoke_runbook.golden_plan\",\"kind\":\"steps\",\"steps\":[\"Validate a capsule file.\",\"Generate a capsule plan.\",\"Confirm referenced use-case and scenario ids resolve.\"],\"observable_outcomes\":[\"The capsule is reusable prepared material whose references resolve.\"]},{\"id\":\"capsule.demos.persisted_smoke_runbook.bad_a_capsule_is_not_proof\",\"kind\":\"steps\",\"steps\":[\"Validate and plan a capsule, then stop.\",\"Read whether anything treats it as proven.\"],\"observable_outcomes\":[\"It is not proof until a run records performed events.\"]},{\"id\":\"capsule.demos.persisted_smoke_runbook.edge_the_same_capsule_serves_repeated_demos\",\"kind\":\"steps\",\"steps\":[\"Plan the same capsule twice without reselecting rows.\",\"Compare the two plans.\"],\"observable_outcomes\":[\"A persisted capsule gives a repeatable demonstration without reselecting rows by hand each time.\"]}],\"observable_outcomes\":[\"The capsule is reusable prepared material.\",\"It is not proof until a run records performed events.\"],\"host_applicability\":[{\"host_surface\":\"codex.cli\",\"supported\":true}],\"verification_policy\":{\"mode\":\"requirements\",\"verifiers\":{\"script\":{\"kind\":\"script\",\"evidence_kind\":\"test_result\",\"command\":[\"pnpm\",\"-s\",\"vitest\",\"run\",\"tests/blackbox/capsule-demos.test.ts\",\"-t\",\"capsule.demos.persisted_smoke_runbook\"],\"inputs\":[\"tests/blackbox/capsule-demos.test.ts\"]}},\"requirements\":[{\"evidence_kind\":\"test_result\",\"required_verifiers\":[\"script\"],\"minimum_count\":1}]},\"approval_policy\":{\"mode\":\"none\"}}","expected_semantic_hash":"sha256:9e9f7f1cd8f1c86ee7f237a6cbc7bc18eb36cd613f0b24e1bbac75451df90b2e"},"result":{"schema_version":1,"operation":"upsert","status":"updated","use_case_id":"capsule.demos.persisted_smoke_runbook","file_path":"use-cases/capsule/demos.yml","before_hash":"sha256:9e9f7f1cd8f1c86ee7f237a6cbc7bc18eb36cd613f0b24e1bbac75451df90b2e","after_hash":"sha256:9e9f7f1cd8f1c86ee7f237a6cbc7bc18eb36cd613f0b24e1bbac75451df90b2e","diagnostics":[]},"written_sha256":"sha256:5620cd256b974bdb219e94389d6ad4bcb08d1ec029f7c80cf78a89b5237ff993","written_length":12595,"written_text":"schema_version: 1\nfeature:\n  id: capsule.demos\n  name: Demo capsules\n  summary: Optional persisted smoke and golden-path runbooks that become proof only when performed as showcase runs.\nuse_cases:\n  - id: capsule.demos.persisted_smoke_runbook\n    title: Persisted smoke demo runbook\n    lifecycle: active\n    value_tier: core\n    journey_role: golden\n    usage_frequency: common\n    tags:\n      - capsules\n      - smoke\n      - runbook\n    source_refs:\n      - kind: file\n        path: docs/showcase.md\n      - kind: file\n        path: packages/core/src/capsules/loadCapsule.ts\n    actor: agent\n    intent: Provide a reusable capsule that references use-case IDs and supports repeatable demos.\n    preconditions:\n      - A common smoke or golden path deserves a persisted runbook.\n    trigger: Agent or user wants a repeatable demonstration without reselecting rows manually.\n    scenarios:\n      - id: capsule.demos.persisted_smoke_runbook.golden_plan\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Validate a capsule file.\n          - Generate a capsule plan.\n          - Confirm referenced use-case and scenario ids resolve.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - The capsule is reusable prepared material whose references resolve.\n      - id: capsule.demos.persisted_smoke_runbook.bad_a_capsule_is_not_proof\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Validate and plan a capsule, then stop.\n          - Read whether anything treats it as proven.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - It is not proof until a run records performed events.\n      - id: capsule.demos.persisted_smoke_runbook.edge_the_same_capsule_serves_repeated_demos\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Plan the same capsule twice without reselecting rows.\n          - Compare the two plans.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - A persisted capsule gives a repeatable demonstration without reselecting rows by hand each time.\n    observable_outcomes:\n      - The capsule is reusable prepared material.\n      - It is not proof until a run records performed events.\n    host_applicability:\n      - host_surface: codex.cli\n        supported: true\n    verification_policy:\n      mode: requirements\n      verifiers:\n        script:\n          kind: script\n          evidence_kind: test_result\n          command:\n            - pnpm\n            - -s\n            - vitest\n            - run\n            - tests/blackbox/capsule-demos.test.ts\n            - -t\n            - capsule.demos.persisted_smoke_runbook\n          inputs:\n            - tests/blackbox/capsule-demos.test.ts\n      requirements:\n        - evidence_kind: test_result\n          required_verifiers:\n            - script\n          minimum_count: 1\n    approval_policy:\n      mode: none\n  - id: capsule.demos.adhoc_release_demo\n    title: Ad hoc release demo plan\n    lifecycle: active\n    value_tier: core\n    journey_role: alternate\n    usage_frequency: occasional\n    tags:\n      - capsules\n      - adhoc\n      - release\n      - no-bad-path\n    source_refs:\n      - kind: file\n        path: docs/showcase.md\n      - kind: file\n        path: packages/core/src/showcase/startRun.ts\n    actor: agent\n    intent: Generate a one-run plan for release proof without saving it as a reusable recipe.\n    preconditions:\n      - The demo is specific to a release, PR, or changed scope.\n    trigger: Agent prepares a one-off live run.\n    scenarios:\n      - id: capsule.demos.adhoc_release_demo.golden_start\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Select ad hoc use-case ids.\n          - Start a showcase run from that selection.\n          - Read the normalized plan recorded in run_started.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - A one-off run records its normalized plan in run_started, so the selection is auditable afterwards.\n      - id: capsule.demos.adhoc_release_demo.edge_no_capsule_file_is_left_behind\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Run a one-off release demo.\n          - Look for a persisted capsule file afterwards.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - One-off demos are supported without accumulating unnecessary capsule files.\n    observable_outcomes:\n      - One-off demos are supported without accumulating unnecessary capsule files.\n    host_applicability:\n      - host_surface: codex.cli\n        supported: true\n    verification_policy:\n      mode: requirements\n      verifiers:\n        script:\n          kind: script\n          evidence_kind: test_result\n          command:\n            - pnpm\n            - -s\n            - vitest\n            - run\n            - tests/blackbox/capsule-demos.test.ts\n            - -t\n            - capsule.demos.adhoc_release_demo\n          inputs:\n            - tests/blackbox/capsule-demos.test.ts\n      requirements:\n        - evidence_kind: test_result\n          required_verifiers:\n            - script\n          minimum_count: 1\n    approval_policy:\n      mode: ask\n  - id: capsule.demos.runner_command_safety\n    title: Hardened scripted capsule execution\n    lifecycle: active\n    value_tier: critical\n    journey_role: negative\n    usage_frequency: common\n    tags:\n      - capsules\n      - command-runner\n      - security\n    source_refs:\n      - kind: file\n        path: packages/core/src/capsules/runCapsule.ts\n      - kind: file\n        path: docs/security.md\n    actor: script\n    intent: Run scripted capsule commands with explicit controls and no committed local-path leakage.\n    preconditions:\n      - A capsule contains command steps.\n    trigger: Agent runs a capsule with command execution enabled.\n    scenarios:\n      - id: capsule.demos.runner_command_safety.golden_command\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Grant command execution permission at both the capsule and the caller level.\n          - Run the capsule and read how each command was executed.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - Commands execute without a shell, from a working directory inside the repo, with bounded output recorded.\n      - id: capsule.demos.runner_command_safety.bad_unsafe_commands_do_not_run_by_default\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Run a capsule containing command steps without granting execution permission.\n          - Read what happens.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - Unsafe commands do not run by default; permission is required at the capsule AND the caller level.\n      - id: capsule.demos.runner_command_safety.bad_working_directory_outside_the_repo\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Point a command step's working directory outside the repository.\n          - Run the capsule.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - The working directory is resolved inside the repo, so a capsule cannot reach out of the workspace.\n      - id: capsule.demos.runner_command_safety.edge_output_is_bounded_and_local_state_does_not_leak\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Run a command producing very large output.\n          - Read what is recorded as the observation and verdict.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - Command results are recorded as observations and verdicts with bounded output, without leaking uncontrolled local state.\n    observable_outcomes:\n      - Unsafe commands do not run by default.\n      - Command results are recorded as observations and verdicts without leaking uncontrolled local state.\n    host_applicability:\n      - host_surface: codex.cli\n        supported: true\n    verification_policy:\n      mode: requirements\n      verifiers:\n        script:\n          kind: script\n          evidence_kind: test_result\n          command:\n            - pnpm\n            - -s\n            - vitest\n            - run\n            - tests/blackbox/capsule-demos.test.ts\n            - -t\n            - capsule.demos.runner_command_safety\n          inputs:\n            - tests/blackbox/capsule-demos.test.ts\n      requirements:\n        - evidence_kind: test_result\n          required_verifiers:\n            - script\n          minimum_count: 1\n    approval_policy:\n      mode: none\n  - id: capsule.demos.stale_reference_warning\n    title: Stale or missing capsule references\n    lifecycle: active\n    value_tier: supporting\n    journey_role: edge\n    usage_frequency: rare\n    tags:\n      - capsules\n      - stale\n      - diagnostics\n    source_refs:\n      - kind: file\n        path: packages/core/src/capsules/loadCapsule.ts\n      - kind: file\n        path: packages/core/src/capsules/index.ts\n    actor: agent\n    intent: Warn when a persisted capsule points at missing, removed, or semantically changed rows.\n    preconditions:\n      - A capsule references use-case or scenario IDs.\n    trigger: Agent validates or plans a capsule after matrix changes.\n    scenarios:\n      - id: capsule.demos.stale_reference_warning.golden_validate\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Validate a capsule after related rows changed.\n          - Read the diagnostics.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - Diagnostics are reported before the capsule is run.\n      - id: capsule.demos.stale_reference_warning.bad_missing_row_reference\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Remove a row a capsule references, then validate the capsule.\n          - Read what is reported.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - A capsule pointing at a missing or removed row is reported rather than run.\n      - id: capsule.demos.stale_reference_warning.edge_semantically_changed_row\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Change a referenced row's meaning without removing it, then validate.\n          - Read whether the drift is detected.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - Persisted runbooks do not silently drift away from the matrix when a row changes underneath them.\n    observable_outcomes:\n      - Persisted runbooks do not silently drift away from the matrix.\n    host_applicability:\n      - host_surface: codex.cli\n        supported: true\n    verification_policy:\n      mode: requirements\n      verifiers:\n        script:\n          kind: script\n          evidence_kind: test_result\n          command:\n            - pnpm\n            - -s\n            - vitest\n            - run\n            - tests/blackbox/capsule-demos.test.ts\n            - -t\n            - capsule.demos.stale_reference_warning\n          inputs:\n            - tests/blackbox/capsule-demos.test.ts\n      requirements:\n        - evidence_kind: test_result\n          required_verifiers:\n            - script\n          minimum_count: 1\n    approval_policy:\n      mode: none\n  - id: capsule.demos.runbook_not_proof\n    title: Capsule is runbook, not proof\n    lifecycle: active\n    value_tier: critical\n    journey_role: negative\n    usage_frequency: common\n    tags:\n      - capsules\n      - proof-boundary\n      - no-edge-path\n    source_refs:\n      - kind: file\n        path: docs/showcase.md\n      - kind: file\n        path: packages/core/src/capsules/runCapsule.ts\n    actor: agent\n    intent: Never treat a persisted or generated capsule as evidence until a live run records events.\n    preconditions:\n      - A capsule exists or a capsule plan has been generated.\n    trigger: Agent summarizes proof, readiness, or release state.\n    scenarios:\n      - id: capsule.demos.runbook_not_proof.golden_guard\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Inspect a capsule or a generated capsule plan.\n          - Read how it describes itself.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - It is reported as prepared material.\n      - id: capsule.demos.runbook_not_proof.bad_a_capsule_never_becomes_evidence\n        kind: steps\n        steps:\n          - Summarise proof, readiness or release state with only a capsule present.\n          - Read whether the capsule counts.\n        observable_outcomes:\n          - Capsule files are not confused with performed demonstrations.\n          - Showcase run events are required before proof is claimed.\n    observable_outcomes:\n      - Capsule files are not confused with performed demonstrations.\n    host_applicability:\n      - host_surface: codex.cli\n        supported: true\n    verification_policy:\n      mode: requirements\n      verifiers:\n        script:\n          kind: script\n          evidence_kind: test_result\n          command:\n            - pnpm\n            - -s\n            - vitest\n            - run\n            - tests/blackbox/capsule-demos.test.ts\n            - -t\n            - capsule.demos.runbook_not_proof\n          inputs:\n            - tests/blackbox/capsule-demos.test.ts\n      requirements:\n        - evidence_kind: test_result\n          required_verifiers:\n            - script\n          minimum_count: 1\n    approval_policy:\n      mode: none\n","unchanged_from_input":true},{"path":"use-cases/capsule/demos.yml","kind":"one_field","options":{"operation":"upsert","target_file":"capsule/demos.yml","use_case_json":"{\"id\":\"capsule.demos.persisted_smoke_runbook\",\"title\":\"Persisted smoke demo runbook (edited)\",\"lifecycle\":\"active\",\"value_tier\":\"core\",\"journey_role\":\"golden\",\"usage_frequency\":\"common\",\"tags\":[\"capsules\",\"smoke\",\"runbook\"],\"source_refs\":[{\"kind\":\"file\",\"path\":\"docs/showcase.md\"},{\"kind\":\"file\",\"path\":\"packages/core/src/capsules/loadCapsule.ts\"}],\"actor\":\"agent\",\"intent\":\"Provide a reusable capsule that references use-case IDs and supports repeatable demos.\",\"preconditions\":[\"A common smoke or golden path deserves a persisted runbook.\"],\"trigger\":\"Agent or user wants a repeatable demonstration without reselecting rows manually.\",\"scenarios\":[{\"id\":\"capsule.demos.persisted_smoke_runbook.golden_